' ── THE KEY LINE, AND A FORM THAT IS ONE SCREEN OF SEVERAL (2026-11-08) ────
' The Executor chose "Back/next across screens". Form.hint composes the key line
' from segments, in this order, joined with " · ":
'   page n/m              only when Step.Of > 1
'   ↑↓ row
'   ←→ choose | ←→ move   move, plus "space toggle", when any row is Multi
'   pgup/pgdn scroll      PgUp/PgDn/Home/End already moved the cursor; the
'                         line never said so
'   enter accept          "enter skip" while the Skip button is focused
'   N steps               only when Form.OnEnter names what Enter runs
'   esc cancel | esc back back when Step.At > 1
'   ctrl+c quit           only when Step.Of > 1
'   N more below          when the viewport hides rows (viewport.puml)
' Until 2026-11-11 the back key was shift+tab and Esc always read "cancel":
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wizard-keys.puml.
' Each segment carries a KEEP rank. Wider than the screen, the line drops the
' lowest-ranked segment, again and again (a tie drops the leftmost), and only
' when one segment is left does it clip. Display order never changes.
'   1 pgup/pgdn scroll   2 space toggle, ctrl+c quit   3 ↑↓ row, ←→ choose | ←→ move, N steps
'   4 page n/m, N more below   5 esc cancel   6 esc back
'   9 enter accept — never dropped
' "enter accept" is the e2e anchor (acceptChoicePrompt,
' _spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml), so the way out outlives everything else.
' ADVERSARIAL REVIEW, 2026-11-08: the first version dropped only the scroll
' segment and then clipped, which cut "enter accept" at ≤61 columns on page 2/3.
' Pinned by TestEnterAcceptSurvivesEveryWidthThatCanHoldIt (every width 12-160,
' every step shape, multi rows).
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (One Card). The segments and their KEEP ranks now:
'   page n/m              5, and only while the head draws no chip (owner, O6)
'   ↑↓ row                3
'   ←→ choose | ←→ move   3
'   space toggle          2; "/ filter" takes its place and rank on a
'                         filterable cell (Executor, E14)
'   pgup/pgdn scroll      1
'   enter accept          9; "enter skip" on Skip; "enter close" while the
'                         .env filter types (owner, O4)
'   N steps               3; absent while the filter types: Enter runs nothing
'   esc cancel | esc back 5 | 6; the word reads "clear" while the filter types
'                         or a query stands
'   ctrl+c quit           2
'   N more below          4
' A tie still drops the leftmost, so the page count drops before "esc cancel"
' when both rank 5. While the filter types the line reads
'   [page n/m ·] ↑↓ row · type to narrow · enter close · esc clear · ctrl+c quit
' with "N more below" after it when rows hide.
' The key line starts at column 2 inside the walls and narrows to cw-4
' (keyRoom); unframed it starts at column 0 and takes the full width.
' "enter accept" is still never dropped. The typing filter is the one state
' without it, and no page opens in that state (wizard-keys.puml).
' hintParts, hint and drawHint take the cursor, because the cursor's open list
' decides the filter's segments.
' THE LINE IS PAINTED IN TWO TONES (2026-11-11, W-e). A segment is a key and
' the word for what it does: "enter" and "accept". hintParts returns them
' apart. hint() joins them into the plain line above, which every test and
' e2e still reads. drawHint paints each key bold in the secondary colour, and
' each word and the " · " between in the muted one. `page n/m` and `N more
' below` have no key and are painted as words.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O5): a key draws bold in the terminal's own ink;
' the secondary colour vanished on a white terminal.
' The paint is cut to the plain line's length, piece by piece, so a clipped
' line ends on the same cell in both.
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/step_test.go:
'   TestTheKeyLinePaintsKeysBoldAndWordsGrey
'   TestAClippedKeyLineStillEndsWhereThePlainLineEnds
' THE FORM SAYS WHAT ENTER WILL RUN (2026-11-11, W-j). Form.OnEnter returns
' the actions Enter runs, in order, for the answers as they stand. Two
' places show them.
'   the key line   "N steps" as its own segment right after "enter accept".
'                  The literal "enter accept" is never widened: it is the e2e
'                  anchor, and a segment of its own can be dropped while the
'                  anchor stays.
'   the region     "on enter", then one numbered line per action, in the rows
'                  LEFT under every other region.
' THE REGION TAKES NO ROW FROM ANYTHING. Its height changes with the
' answers. Budgeted above the key line it would move that line on every
' keystroke. Drawn last, in leftover rows, it moves nothing: with too few
' rows it ends on "… and N more", with none it is absent and the count on
' the key line still says how much Enter runs.
' While the Skip button is focused Enter runs nothing, so both go.
' WHO SETS IT: init's setup page, from the plan the apply executes
' (_spec/internal/ui/step-lines.puml), and the run form, from the clone
' decision (_spec/internal/run/run-spec.puml).
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/form_model_test.go:
'   TestTheCountOfWhatEnterRunsFollowsEnterAcceptAndNeverReplacesIt
'   TestTheOnEnterRegionFillsOnlyTheRowsLeftAndNeverMovesTheKeyLine
' Form.Step{At, Of} places a form in a sequence; the zero value is a lone form.
' RunStep returns an Outcome, Accepted | Cancelled | Back, and Run keeps
' (bool, error) as RunStep == Accepted. leave() answers the keys that end a
' form. On a lone form: esc and ctrl+c → Cancelled, enter → Accepted. On a
' wizard's page esc → Back past page 1, ctrl+c → Quit after a question, and
' shift+tab still → Back (wizard-keys.puml); on the first screen shift+tab does
' nothing. `q` is not in leave(): a field takes it as typing first.
' `proveo run` is one form, so only its footer changed. `proveo init` walks
' three: _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml.
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/step_test.go: TestShiftTabStepsBackOnlyPastTheFirstScreen,
' TestHintNamesThePageTheWayBackAndTheScrollKeys,
' TestANarrowHintDropsTheScrollKeysBeforeTheWayOut,
' TestEnterAcceptSurvivesEveryWidthThatCanHoldIt, TestTheDrawnHeadCarriesThePage
' (named TestTheDrawnFooterCarriesThePage until the chip took the page count).

' ── THE DEVICES ROW PACKS; TUI AND DESKTOP ARE ONE RADIO (2026-10-24) ──────
' User: "has empty spaces for browser/android/ios, avoid that. Show chrome and
' desktop directly there … Remove the disabled option in tui (radio button
' style) let the user choose tui or desktop". layoutInterface keeps the
' canonical order (tui, desktop, browser, android, ios, the rest) but packs the
' columns 0..n-1, so a harness without browser/android/ios shows no gaps
' (hermes: (•) tui  ( ) desktop  [ ] chrome). Where a harness offers desktop,
' tui stops being a locked [X]: Row.RadioSet draws tui and desktop as radios
' inside the checkbox row, pairTUIDesktop keeps exactly one on (the newer tick
' wins, an empty radio snaps back), and tui never enters the add-on list.
' Elsewhere tui stays the fixed [X] of addonFixed.
' Pinned by TestTheDevicesRowPacksItsOptionsWithoutGaps,
' TestTUIAndDesktopAreOneRadioChoice (internal/run) and
' TestARadioSetDrawsRadiosBesideCheckboxes (internal/choiceui).
'
' ── THE AUTH ROW IS AN AXIS, AND IT IS ORDERED BY RISK ─────────────────────
' Three options, always drawn in this order, because the prompt labels the row's
' horizontal as "◀ riskier ... safer ▶" and reading it left to right has to mean
' something:
'   usage credits ... metered per token against raw provider key material sitting
'                     in the environment for the agent to read. Unbounded spend,
'                     and the key is a file or a variable the agent can reach.
'   subscription .... a fixed-cost plan credential, and where it is a login on
'                     disk proveo suppresses env tokens over it. The failure this
'                     row exists to stop runs one way only — a subscription run
'                     silently billed per token, never the reverse.
'   local model ..... the safe end. Weights on this machine: nothing billed, and
'                     no credential for the agent or the egress hop to carry.
'                     COMING SOON — `--local-model` already runs the Ollama
'                     sidecar, but nothing routes THIS row to it, so it is drawn
'                     and gated rather than left out. The axis is where an
'                     operator looks to find out an option exists.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O2): no legend labels a row any more. The order
' stays: the egress and model columns still run riskier to safer, left to
' right. What the order lost is the caption that claimed it.
'
' AN UNAVAILABLE OPTION IS GATED, NEVER DROPPED. cursor's CLI has no
' bring-your-own-key path, so "usage credits" is off with the reason attached —
' dropping it is what made "cursor ignores my ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" something the
' operator could only discover by running. The reason goes in OffWhy, per option,
' so it appears under the option the cursor is on rather than as one row-wide
' string; Reason keeps the joined form for the row.
'
' comingSoon is NOT used here. It reallocates Off on every call, so gating two of
' three through it silently un-gates the first — the auth row gates its own
' options and picks a new Selected when the remembered one landed on a gate.
'
' AND A GATED OPTION ON A SINGLE-SELECT ROW EXPLAINS ITSELF THROUGH Reason, NOT
' OffWhy. cycle() skips an Off option on a single-select row — correctly, it
' cannot be chosen — so the cursor never lands on it and the per-option OffWhy
' is text nothing will ever display. helpLines suppressed the row-level Reason
' the moment the row carried any Help, which is exactly the shape of the auth
' row: cursor drew `usage credits` greyed out and said NOTHING about why, the
' one thing drawing it was supposed to communicate. The egress row escaped this
' only by carrying no Help map.
'
' A Multi row is not affected and keeps its old behaviour: cycle() moves onto
' gated options there and toggle() refuses, so its OffWhy is reachable and
' repeating Reason beside it would double the add-on rows up.
'
' THE HINT IS THE HALF THAT MAKES THE NOUNS MEAN SOMETHING. Under each option:
' what it is, then what it is made of on THIS host — host env variable names and
' the login file path when a login is what will be spent — then what choosing it
' withholds. It does not name a project .env: that file is not a credential
' surface. SPEC: _spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O4): the credentials row's .env cell is a
' names-only inventory of p.HostEnvFile. Its help is the one place the form
' names that file; an auth option's hint still never does. The login path in
' a hint and in a gate's reason is now shortened with ~ (Executor, review
' fix 8).
'
title Choice prompt wireframe — one card, and how a gated element is drawn

