{
{^"1 · fixed — read-only inventory, four classes"
  credentials | <color:#9a9a9a>[X] API keys ▾</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>[X] OAuth ▾</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>[X] SSH ▾</color> | <color:#9a9a9a>[X] .env ▾</color>
  .
  Left/right opens each populated class.
  Up/down traverses its complete list.
  Space never changes a credential.
  Empty classes stay unticked without
  an arrow. Counts describe the host
  inventory; model and kit bindings
  determine which entries a run uses.
  .
  .env (2026-11-13, owner O4) lists the
  names the run's env file sets: names
  only, A to Z, no tick boxes, and "/"
  filters them. A run with no env file
  draws the cell unticked, with no arrow.
}
{^"2 · empty cell — option withdrawn"
  model | ( ) Qwen 3.8 | (X) API keys | . | ( ) Glimmer
  .
  The slot persists, so surviving options
  retain the column they occupied while
  the full complement was offered.
  A harness without a plan leaves its
  model-source column empty.
}
{^"3 · absent region — applicableRows"
  ├── reach ────── | . | . | . | .
  mcp | ( ) on | (X) off | . | .
  .
  A row with nothing to determine is
  eliminated wholesale. Its section's stub
  moves to the first row that survives,
  here mcp when egress is unreadable. A
  section with no rows draws no stub.
  Until 2026-11-13 a riskier/safer legend
  sat above these rows; no form draws it.
}
{^"4 · one answer — a radio, not a gated pair"
  outputs | ( ) filtered | (X) verbose
  execution | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | (X) <color:#9a9a9a>sandbox</color>
  .
  Brackets say "any number of these" and
  parentheses "one of these". Evidence is
  genuinely one-of, so it is a radio row and
  the gate that kept two boxes exclusive —
  leaving "neither" reachable — is gone.
  .
  Execution is one-of by construction (a run
  has one place it runs) and now carries ONE
  box: the sidecar that made "neither" reachable
  is retired, so the row is greyed and ticked —
  a fact, not a question.
}
{^"5 · filtered — the bridge never reads it"
  set by operator | <color:#00BAC6>ARCHITECT_MODEL</color> | <color:#9a9a9a><s>EDITOR_MODEL</s></color> | <color:#00BAC6>SMALL_MODEL</color>
  claudecode reads | <color:#00BAC6>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</color> | . | <color:#00BAC6>ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL</color>
  prompt shows | <color:#00BAC6>main=</color> | . | <color:#00BAC6>small=</color>
  .
  Claude Code routes internally and exposes two slots, so ""EDITOR_MODEL"" is a
  fallback that never fires once ""ARCHITECT_MODEL"" is set. Printing all three
  role vars advertises an assignment the harness cannot honour, so the header
  shows the resolved slots instead — and every slot it shows is highlighted,
  because a half-highlighted row reads as one model mattering more than another.
}
{^"7 · described — the cursor's option explains itself, under the card"
  devices | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui</color> | [X] browser | [ ] android | <back:#8A8A8A>[ ] <s>ios</s></back>
  ↑↓ row · ←→ move · space toggle · pgup/pgdn scroll · enter accept · esc cancel | . | . | .
  <color:#00BAC6>› ios — an iOS Simulator on this host — coming soon</color> | . | . | .
  <b>off:</b> coming soon — not built yet | . | . | .
  .
  The picker could only ever explain what it had taken AWAY: ""Reason"" is written
  when an option is gated off, so the add-ons that were available and ticked
  carried no text and "browser" had to be inferred from its name.
  ""Help"" describes the option the CURSOR is on, one row at a time — describing
  every option of every row at once is the wall of text this replaces.

  WRAPPED, never appended to the row: the row is already ~70 columns of
  checkboxes, so text placed after them runs off the terminal, which is how the
  one description the picker did have ended mid-sentence. The row's own
  ""Reason"" is still drawn inline and is now clipped with an ellipsis — it is a
  glance signal for a row the cursor is not on, and the same words are here in
  full.

  **Pinned LAST, under the hint, with nothing drawn after it.** Under its own row
  the block's height changed with the cursor and shoved every row beneath it up
  and down — the form moved while the operator was reading it. At the bottom it
  can grow freely and nothing above ever shifts. Since 2026-11-13 the card's
  bottom border sits between the key line and the help.

  A greyed box that is TICKED reads "always on:" rather than "off:": it is not
  unavailable, it is compulsory, and the other label would say the opposite of
  what the checkbox shows. The head draws bold; lime left the help.
}
{^"8 · fixed — a box that states a fact"
  execution | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | (X) <color:#9a9a9a>sandbox</color> | .
  devices | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui</color> | [ ] browser | [ ] android | [ ] ios
  .
  Greyed, and left in the state it states. ""host"" is the alternative an operator
  might otherwise assume unticking the daemon selects — it never is, because
  proveo containerises every run — and the TUI is the interface for the whole
  session whether or not a browser joins it. Neither is reported as a selected
  add-on, and neither appears in the row's inline ""Reason"": a note greyed on
  every run teaches the operator to skip the line that sometimes matters.

  **The sandbox is greyed for the opposite reason: it is COMPULSORY.** A harness
  that declares sbx runs there and nowhere else, so the box is ticked and locked
  and its help line reads "always on: Mount the current git project in a
  sandbox for the agent". Unticking used to reach the docker backend behind egress
  sidecars — a weaker boundary one keystroke away — and that escape then became
  ""PROVEO_SBX=0"". Since 2026-10-16 there is no escape: the docker backend is
  deleted, and since 2026-10-17 ""PROVEO_SBX"" is simply unread. Like the
  two facts above it stays out of the row's inline ""Reason"": a note greyed on
  every run only teaches the operator to skip the line that sometimes matters.

  It is the one greyed box that IS reported as a selected add-on. ""Selections""
  drops every greyed option, which is right for the two facts above and wrong
  here: a compulsory sandbox dropped from the read-back once sent the run to
  the very backend the lock existed to remove; that backend is now deleted.
  Since 2026-11-13 the terminal draws such an answer FIXED (plain ink) and an
  unavailable one GATED (faint, struck); salt keeps grey for both.
}
{^"6 · nerd, fallback ascii — PROVEO_GLYPHS"
  The per-language devicons of the ""lsp:"" header row left with that row
  (2026-10-30, LSP removal). The tiers still decorate status marks.
  .
  Devicons live in a range a Powerline-patched font does not carry, and a terminal
  cannot be asked whether its font holds a codepoint — so nerd is the tier an
  operator declares with ""=nerd"", and the undeclared default falls back to
  Safe, never to a guess autodetection makes.
  .
  The card's frame follows the tier: rounded corners and tees on nerd and
  safe; plus signs, hyphens and bars on ascii and off.
}
{^"9 · model — one row: where the model comes from (every harness)"
  model | ( ) Qwen 3.8 | (X) API keys | ( ) plan | ( ) Glimmer
  <color:#00BAC6>› Qwen 3.8 — 27B, MLX, same as --local-model qwen3.8:27b-mlx on darwin/arm64</color> | . | . | . | .
  .
  ONE row picks the model source (2026-09-27). It merges what used to be two:
  the auth row (""usage credits"" · ""subscription"", drawn for a harness with a
  plan) and the local-model row. ""usage credits"" is drawn as ""API keys"" and
