legend bottom
  <color:#9a9a9a>grey text</color> — not selectable: the terminal draws a FIXED answer in plain ink and a locked row's label faint; salt grey is not the terminal's grey
  <color:#9a9a9a><s>grey, struck</s></color> — unavailable (gated): the terminal draws it faint and struck through
  <s>struck</s> — cleared by a cross-row gate, or never read by this harness
  plain text — offered and selectable: the terminal draws it grey (#8A8A8A), and bold once chosen
  <back:#00BAC6>a cyan fill</back> — the cursor's answer, black on brand; <back:#8A8A8A>a grey fill</back> — the cursor on a fixed or unavailable answer
  <back:#0E3A48><color:#00BAC6> chip </color></back> — the step chip, brand on the surface colour; it owns the page count
  ├── name ── — a section's stub; the cursor's section draws its stub and its left wall in brand, its name bold
  the box around the form — the card: ╭─╮ walls ├─┤ ╰─╯, min(w, 120) wide; ascii and off draw plus signs, hyphens and bars
  a "." cell — element absent, column position preserved for the survivors
  a titled group box — region rendered only while its title predicate holds
  no frame whatsoever — no TTY, so the form is never drawn and resolved values stand
  a glyph before a label — accented marker; devicon by default, ASCII via PROVEO_GLYPHS=ascii
  a "›" line under the card — what the option the cursor is on does, wrapped; "off:" adds why it cannot be picked
end legend
